Our scene-conditioned evaluation clarifies this tradeoff. Figure [15](https://ar5iv.labs.arxiv.org/html/2605.30578#S5.F15 "Figure 15 ‣ 5.4.5. Impact of ℓ₂ Regularization ‣ 5.4. Effectiveness of Physical Attack Techniques ‣ 5. Evaluation ‣ AdvScene: Rethinking Adversarial Patch Evaluation Through Scene Robustness") shows that adding ℓ2\ell\_{2} regularization does not substantially degrade deployed attack performance within the operational envelope. The curves for no, low, medium, and high ℓ2\ell\_{2} regularization largely overlap, indicating that the operational envelope is not determined by the pixel-level magnitude constraint. Although ℓ2\ell\_{2} changes the optimized patch appearance and may slightly affect anchor-view performance, its effect is much weaker than scene-induced factors such as projected footprint, visibility, and viewing geometry.

